PKGMAN-DSEARCH(1) "@PACKAGE_STRING@"

# NAME

pkgman-dsearch - search package source directories for package names \
and descriptions

# SYNOPSIS

*pkgman dsearch* [*-v* | *-vv*] [*--path*] [*--regex*] _expr_

# DESCRIPTION

The *pkgman dsearch* command searches the package source directories
listed by the *pkgsrcdir* directive in *pkgman.conf*(5) for _expr_ in
package names and descriptions.

The _expr_ argument may be a plain string, or a regular expression in
*regex*(3) format.

The options are as follows:

*-v*
	Include the package version in the listing.

*-vv*
	Include the package version and description in the listing.

*--path*
	Include the package source path in the listing.

*--regex*
	Interpret _expr_ as a regular expression.

# EXIT STATUS

*0*
	Matches found.
*>0*
	No matches found, or an error occurred.

# EXAMPLES

Search package names and descriptions for the word "network":
```
pkgman dsearch -vv network
```

Search package names or descriptions for "server" or "daemon":
```
pkgman dsearch -vv --regex 'server|daemon'
```

# SEE ALSO

*pkgman-search*(1),
*pkgman-fsearch*(1),
*pkgman*(1),
*pkgman.conf*(5),
*regex*(3)

